<main class="pc" data-product-depth="logbook"><p class="pc-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / Research / Research logbook</p><h1>How the system learns.</h1><p class="pc-lead">The engineering logbook connects open questions, models, prototypes and subsequent verification.</p><div class="pc-steps" role="navigation" aria-label="Research"><a href="../primordocciput/">Primordocciput</a><a href="../c0-c1/">C0–C1–C2</a><a href="../logbook/" aria-current="page">Logbook</a></div><section class="pc-section"><h2>Working register</h2><p class="pc-note">A register of existing materials, not results from new experiments.</p><div class="pc-grid"><article class="pc-card"><p class="pc-kicker">Technology demonstration</p><h3>Vita Wellness</h3><p>Separate L/R representation and longitudinal change.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../../technology/vita-wellness/">Vita Wellness ↗</a></article><article class="pc-card"><p class="pc-kicker">Research concept</p><h3>Primordocciput</h3><p>Definition of a reference and a way to test it.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../primordocciput/">Primordocciput ↗</a></article><article class="pc-card"><p class="pc-kicker">Interactive illustration</p><h3>Configuration</h3><p>Independent components of head orientation.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../configuration/">Configuration ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="pc-section"><h2>Four kinds of research information</h2><div class="pc-grid"><details class="pc-card"><summary>Observed</summary><p>Describe what is visible in a particular context.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Measured</summary><p>Record units, method, conditions and uncertainty.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Reported</summary><p>Preserve the source of the subjective report.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Research concept</summary><p>State the model, question and possible test.</p></details></div><div class="pc-actions"><a class="pc-button primary" href="../start/">Discuss research collaboration</a><a class="pc-button" href="../technology/">Technology</a></div></section><section class="pc-section"><details class="pc-legacy"><summary>Existing materials</summary><div class="wrap"><article class="article"><div class="crumbs">CRANIO / Engineer’s Logbook</div><h2>Show how CRANIO learns.</h2><p class="lead">Observations, experiments, geometry, anatomy, comparisons and open questions.</p><section class="section"><div class="eyebrow">Engineer’s Logbook</div><h2>Show how CRANIO learns.</h2><p class="lead">Observations, experiments, geometry, anatomy, comparisons and open questions.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>Observation</h3><p>Separate observation from interpretation.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Context</h3><p>Context makes a state comparable over time.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Verification</h3><p>Before, after, context and time remain visible.</p></div></div></section><div class="actions"><a class="btn dark" href="../start/">Start an observation</a><a class="btn" href="../explore/">Explore</a></div></article></div></details></section></main>